    [Doc] Update pipeline parallel feature compatibility matrices (#19589)
    
    ### What this PR does / why we need it?
    
    The feature matrix still marks several supported PP combinations as
    unknown and states that PP graph mode only supports `FULL_DECODE_ONLY`.
    Update both the general feature matrix and the PP guide to document
    support for piecewise ACL graphs, KV Cache Pool, LM head TP, MLAPO,
    multimodal inputs, multistream MoE, shared expert DP, quantization, and
    NZ weights.
    
    Mark all existing quantization columns (W4A4, W4A8, and W8A8) as
    compatible with PP, and document that PP supports all quantization
    methods available for the model and hardware. Remove the obsolete
    graph-mode restriction and clarify that the entries describe individual
    feature combinations with PP.
    
    ### Does this PR introduce _any_ user-facing change?
    
    No runtime behavior changes. This is a documentation-only update; no
    release note fragment is required.
    
    ### How was this patch tested?
    
    - `bash format.sh ci` — all checks passed.
    - `git diff --check` and `git diff --cached --check` — passed before
    committing.
    - Parsed the general matrix to verify that all 28 table rows align to 26
    columns, all requested PP entries show support, and footnote references
    match their definitions.
    - Checked consistency with the PP guide and verified that unrelated
    compatibility cells and existing model-specific limitations are
    preserved.
    - Confirmed that only the two Markdown files changed; no `.po` updates.
    
    No runtime tests were added because this change only updates
    documentation. No new NPU inference or performance tests were run.
    
